Governor Hirofumi Yoshimura (45) of Osaka Prefecture made a remote appearance from the prefectural office on ABC TV “Cast” in Osaka (Monday to Friday, March 48) on the 20th, and said that as part of measures to prevent the spread of the new coronavirus infection, he is considering a partnership with the restaurant information website “Gurunavi”.
Since the beginning of this month, Osaka Prefecture has issued an "infection prevention declaration sticker" to businesses that comply with the guidelines in order to promote efforts to prevent the spread of infection and provide peace of mind to citizens.
However, more than one hundred and twenty thousand shops at restaurants are said to issue stickers.
Therefore, Governor Yoshimura said, “I’m going to do it at the end of the month, but when I make a reservation, I’m going to partner with ‘Gurunabi’, and when I make a reservation, I’m going to open the issuing store of the declaration sticker so that I can understand it at the reservation stage,” and declared a tag with the Internet reservation site.
“The most important thing is not to lump it together with the ‘night city’. You should properly and clearly separate the shops that you are dealing with infectious diseases. It is also important to make an effort to increase the number of stores that will do it,” he said.
