From the 25th, a special exhibition "History and Culture Exhibition of Toyosawa Town" will be held at Kenji's Square in Kamimachi, Hanamaki City.
Kenji Miyazawa (1896-1933), a poet and fairy tale writer, exhibited a notebook with the residents of Toyosawa-cho, the same city where he grew up, writing that he had sent relief money to the affected areas affected by the Great Kanto Earthquake in 23 (Taisho 12).
It is a valuable material that shows the connection between Kenji and Toyosawa-cho, and introduces it together with the culture and history of the town.
Until August 23rd.
The notebook was discovered when Yuji Ito, 60, a member of the promotion association and a group employee in Toyosawa-cho, the same city, organized the warehouse at his home last summer.
It was used by his father-in-law Genzo TAKAHASHI (1900-85), who ran a local general store.
On September 15th, it was written as “Tokyo City Earthquake Relief Money Wanted (Residential Soldiers)”, and along with the symbols “ ○” and “×”, the names of Kenji and the residents of Toyosawa Town at that time, and the amount of donations are written.
