Immediate detection of a crisis outbreak from the Internet information and judgment of a hoax (JBpress) - Yahoo! News
“I want to know as soon as possible what kind of disasters and accidents occurred!”
This has strong needs not only in news organizations such as televisions and newspapers, but also in many companies such as social infrastructure companies and local governments.
The service that responds to this is "Specty" developed by Spectee, which is engaged in information analysis using AI.
[Photo] An alert from Specty determines the authenticity of social media information
Now, the first way for people to know about disasters and accidents has begun to shift from TV to social media.
Social media, such as Twitter, has become an important medium for disseminating information immediately after a disaster or accident occurs.
However, it is difficult by hand to constantly watch overflowing information and extracting useful information from them.
Specty has the function of detecting things related to natural disasters and accidents from information flowing on social media such as Twitter, Instagram, Facebook, etc., analyzes the contents, determines the authenticity of the information, and distributes it to the user's company.
"It is a crisis management support service that visualizes various crises occurring both in Japan and overseas, with a wide range of "crisises" such as events with negative impacts such as suspending or stagnating social activities."
At the time of the Kumamoto earthquake in April, NHK was the first major use case of Specty, after which the recruitment movement spread rapidly among companies.
More than three hundred and fifty companies in Japan, not only TV stations and newspapers, but also companies that support social infrastructure such as electricity, gas, and transportation, and local governments across the country are currently using Specty.
■ Analyzing posts to determine the type and location of the “crisis”
Specty distributes information through four steps: “information collection,” “analysis and content classification,” “title,” and “true judgment.”
Employers should specify in advance the areas where they collect information (prefectures, municipalities, etc.) and the categories of crises (disasters, accidents, etc.).
Specty uses the API provided by social media to collect posts that fall under that designation.
Next, we will analyze the text, images, and videos contained in the collected posts and classify them.
For example, if there is a video showing a fire engine, black smoke rising from the building, and an orange flame coming out of the room, it will be classified as a “fire”.
In addition, images of overturned cars are classified as “traffic accidents”, and images of roads covered with water are classified like “road flooding”.
Specty will also estimate the location of disasters and accidents.
"We often don't know the location from the post, so we estimate it by combining various information," says CEO Murakami.
For example, if there are road signs and signs reflected in images and videos, information on place names can be extracted from it, collated with the place name database, and the location can be identified.
