"Cold Noodle Cooking" Unpopular (Contemporary Business) - Yahoo! News
Chilled Chinese in China is "Nichi-style cold noodles".
As mentioned at the beginning, chilled Chinese is a Chinese cuisine (Japanese-style Chinese) originated in Japan, conceived based on China's "Ryangumien" (Lyangbammien / chilled mixed buckwheat noodles).
Therefore, it does not originally exist in China, but due to the diversification of food, it has come to be seen at Japanese restaurants in the summer.
Recently, Japanese convenience stores have also introduced arranged products under the name "Nikshiki Soba Ryomen / Soba Cold Chinese" and "Kawakodori Goryomen / Sichuan-Furi Chiroshi Chuka".
On the other hand, due to popular Chinese dishes such as Sichuan cuisine and Hunan cuisine, the popularity of Japanese-style Chinese in China is generally not high.
Needless to say, the seasoning of Japanese-style Chinese is often familiar even to Chinese people.
That's why I don't feel bad, but if I have a poor impact, I tend to be harshly criticized.
"Cold China" is no exception, and it is still a minor existence in China.
By the way, the name of chilled Chinese in China is "Nichishiki cold noodles".
The Chinese are recognized as one of Japanese cuisine.
The standard of the summer is "Ryampy"
In China, when it comes to noodle dishes with a sense of summer, I don’t think it’s “Ryampi”.
In Japan, I think that there are many people who are not familiar with it, but the cool skin is flat noodles made from flour, rice flour, starch, etc. originating in Shaanxi Province.
It is said to have a history of two thousand years.
It is a classic B-grade gourmet that is also sold at food stalls, and the price is around 10 to 20 yuan (150 to 300 yen), which is very reasonable.
There is a letter "涼" in it, but like cold Chinese in Japan, it is not covered with ice.
Rather, room temperature is basic.
On top of the noodles, topped with favorite ingredients such as shredded cucumbers, carrots, boiled bean sprouts, and other condiments such as coak, chili pepper, ginger, and garlic are added.
At the end, a mixture of soy sauce, oil, vinegar, sesama paste, peanut paste, etc. are mixed with a special seasoning.
Noodles that have a good throat and are pulled down, the sourness is refreshing, and the thick spicy sauce is well entangled, and even when there is no appetite due to the feeling of summer fatigue, it will enter smoothly.
In addition, since it has penetrated throughout China, there are various toppings and seasonings, and there are plenty of variations, which is one of the characteristics of cool skin, and it is one of the ways to enjoy it.
