Online Museum "HASARD" Mr. Konno (from Hachinohe) Launched (Daily Tohoku Shimbun) - Yahoo! News
There is a museum where everyone can experience art for free whenever they want.
From famous painters such as Claude Monet and Gustav Klimt to unknown artists in Japan.
Since its "opening" in April, the online museum "HASARD" has captured the hearts of its users from its convenience and newness, and with a new lifestyle due to the coronavirus pandemic, the level of attention has increased further.
Shinnosuke Konno (26), a representative from Hachinohe City who started the site, said, "I wanted to create a service where everyone can easily enjoy art. I want them to be exposed to art under difficult circumstances."
When you visit Azar, you will be surprised by the abundance of the exhibits and the beauty of the images.
As of the 24th, a total of fourteen permanent exhibitions and special exhibitions have been released, attracting people to see ultra-high-resolution works that convey not only the color but also the texture of the brush.
There is no need to register as a member or an entrance fee, and not only the viewer, but also the artist who wants to open a solo exhibition does not cost anything.
The way they appear online also attracts attention.
Moving a painting is one of them.
Claude Monet's permanent exhibition "It Begins to Move Again" has been digitally processed so that clouds, flowers, grasslands, etc. can move.
"I want people who are not interested in art to be able to enter" (Representative of Konno), so you can enjoy the feeling of being in a picture.
When I was in elementary school, I met art with Mr. Konno.
At that time, when I visited with my family at the Aomori Prefectural Museum of Art, which had just been completed, I saw three huge pictures of Marc Chagall's "Areco" and I was shocked by its power.
From the next day, art classes changed to a fun time, and even after entering university, he began to visit galleries and other places.
At the same time, I felt that there are many people who do not have the opportunity to interact with art from various perspectives, such as the fact that there are no museums nearby, large exhibitions are held in the Tokyo metropolitan area, and it is difficult to go out due to childcare.
Therefore, while working for an IT company, he spent about two months launching a site where he could appreciate art on the Internet.
The number of users reached an average of ten thousand per month in the first ten months, and since the spread of the new coronavirus, it has increased to about thirty thousand.
If you can appreciate art in a free way when you want to see it.
Azar's aim has been accepted by as many people as possible due to the coronavirus pandemic.
Mr. Konno emphasized that it enriches his imagination with regard to the significance of art appreciation.
“When you’re imaginative, you’ll be able to reach out to people in need.
I want art to become a better society by becoming familiar with it.”
A simple reason why the era of Chinese quality has ended and the era of Japanese quality is coming (modern business) - Yahoo! News
Change of values during the pandemic
There are various predictions and discussions about the after-pandemic world.
In terms of business, there is a possibility of a change mentioned in the July 8th article “In fact, the work of “management” is now disappearing in Japan ...! The cruel reality” and the July 4th article “In the world of “post-coronavirus”, in fact, ‘Japan’s manufacturing industry’ is likely to make a big comeback ...!”
[Photo] The true identity of "Japan's strength" that only Japanese people do not know ... The unexpected reality seen in Asia
In addition, in terms of spirit, it seems that the flow of the June 26th article, "To give to people who have come to be aware of the end of their lives due to the corona", the June 10th article "Corona, let's look at the utility of "God in times of distress" now full of riots" will become the mainstream.
In addition, what seems to be clearly visible to our eyes as a form where these two “materials (economy and business)” and “spirit” come together, is a major trend from “Chinese quality to Japanese quality”.
For example, it is infuriating if there are defects or defects in T-shirts and digital cameras, but there is no separate article on the lives of the person who bought it.
On the other hand, the sloppy quality of Chinese-made masks and ventilators, which has recently become a hot topic, is fatal in products that are directly linked to life and safety.
No matter how cheap it is, you can't buy such products.
Even if you pay a considerable price, you will ask for "Japanese quality" products.
Of course, this trend is not only happening in Japan.
It is also clear from the fact that Western countries in a difficult situation due to the shortage of masks and medical devices made "returns" one after another due to "Chinese quality".
Safer and more secure than safety.
In addition, products such as automobiles are also products whose defects can be fatal (deaths due to accidents).
No matter how many countries, including China and South Korea, go on the offensive with the low-selling strategy of "Let's do evil", it will not be able to compete with Japanese products in the end, and in the June 16th article "Do you win alone, will the world's automakers bow down to Toyota?", because "Japanese quality" is strongly required for automobile products.
And this pandemic reminded me of the need for “safety and security” for many other products.
In addition, safety and security are important not only in "Japanese quality in manufacturing" but also in "Japanese quality in services such as logistics".
Like toilet paper riots, there are times when the production capacity is proper, but the intermediate distribution is stalled and it can not be reached.
Furthermore, on April 17th, like the article "Who is the real culprit of the shortage of masks! Don't allow the fire site thief of the Chinese Communist Party regime", self-sufficiency in Japan is also keenly aware that it is an important element of "safety and security".
In the event of an emergency, it is natural for every country to take precedence, and it is very important to be able to procure essential items such as masks (medical equipment) and food at home.
South Korea's new coronavirus cases exceed 100 for the first time in 115 days (Yonhap News) - Yahoo! News
NEW YORK (Reuters) - South Korea's central anti-epidemic headquarters said on Tuesday that the number of people infected with the new coronavirus as of midnight on this day had risen to 113 as of midnight on the previous day, bringing the total number to 14092.
The number of new infections per day has surpassed one hundred for the first time in 115 days since April 1.
Thirty-two of the 293 workers who returned from Iraq on the 24th have tested positive, in addition to the infection of thirty-two Russian ships entering the port of Busan.
The number of new infections in South Korea stood at thirty to sixty, with the exception of twenty-six.
Eighty-six of the new infections announced on the 25th, eighty-six people have entered from overseas, the highest number since January 20th, when the first infected person in South Korea came out.
Thirty-six people came from Iraq, thirty-four from Russia, five from the Philippines, and three from the United States.
Twenty-seven people have been confirmed infected, including eleven in Seoul and Gyeonggi-do, respectively, and five in Busan.
Five people in the city of Busan were employees of a repairman on board a Russian vessel.
The death toll remained unchanged from the previous day, totaling 298 people.
