Akio Kinoshita, ophthalmology director of Hiramatsu Hospital, explaining dry eyes, etc. = Yonezawa Saga Main Store of Glasses in Saga City
Mr. Akio Kinoshita, Director of Ophthalmology at Hiramatsu Hospital, explained the dry eye, "Hot Seminar" = Yonezawa Saga Main Store of Glasses in Saga City
On the 25th, an expert gave advice on various health-related health-related health-related health-related issues (sponsored by the Saga Shimbun and co-sponsored by Yonezawa of Glasses) was held at the Yonezawa Saga head office in Shimoda-cho, Saga City.
Akio Kinoshita, director of ophthalmology at Hiramatsu Hospital (Ogi City), explained the diseases of the eyes deeply related to daily life, such as dry eyes and cataracts.
Dry eye is said to be a "sickness of tears", explaining that the quality of tears collapses, and tears do not spread evenly on the surface of the eyes.
Kinoshita said, “Contact lens users are about four times more likely,” and cautioned, “Don’t use it for a long time or sleep while wearing it.”
It showed measures such as placing the computer's screen lower than the height of the eye, and humidifying it in a room where the air conditioner worked.
We also introduced ingredients and foods that are effective for dry eyes.
"Omega-3s, which are contained in blue fish, prevent the evaporation of tears, and 'mucin', which is found in a lot of natto and okra, enhances the quality of tears," he said.
For cataract surgery, there was a monofocal and multi-focal on the intraocular lens inserted instead of the crystalline lens, and the difference in appearance was touched.
About forty people attended the seminar.
