Progress toward branded pigs Minoru pork acquired JGAP (Daily Tohoku Shimbun) - Yahoo! News
On the 20th, Minoru Nakano, the president of Towada City, which breeds about fifty thousand pigs a year at farms in Towada City and Rokunohe Town, visited Mayor Hisashi Oyamada at Towada City Hall and reported that the company's farm had acquired "JGAP (livestock and livestock products) certification," which indicates the safety of agricultural and livestock products.
It is the second case as a pig farming company in the prefecture.
The company is engaged in the production of “garlic pork” that uses powder from the prefecture’s garlic as a special feed, and “jitan”, which uses local rice produced in the prefecture.
This time, out of the five farms, about ten thousand were raised and JGAP certification was obtained at the fifth farm (Rokunohe-cho), which produces "local pig".
The company decided to acquire the certification because it learned that it is necessary to obtain certification by major buyers, and that it has become a condition to procure the ingredients used in the Olympic Village at the Tokyo Olympics.
Since August last year, with the support of the Aomori Bank, preparations have been made with JGAP's qualified staff.
On March 3rd of this year, it was examined by the certification body, and cleared a total of 113 items such as food safety.
It was certified on the 13th of the same month.
On this day's visit, the company's representative Minoru Nakano, Mr. Watari Nakano, Mr. Wataru Nakano, Mr. Takeo YAMADA and Mr. Minami Towada of the Aomori Bank, and Mr. Yoshihiro Ishigo of the bank's corporate support department attended the meeting.
Mayor Oyamada said, "It's really great. I want you to do a lot of PR (JGAP certification) and lead to the expansion of sales channels."
"I would like to continue to contribute to Towada City by making efforts to brand pork," said Minoru Nakano, the company's representative.
"We are aiming to obtain certification for the remaining four farms," said Mr. Nakano, managing director.
