A circle of light, a horizontal rainbow co-stars Yamagata, Nikki and the circular horizontal ark observed|Yamagata Shimbun
At the same time, a horizontal rainbow-coloured ring arc appeared under the sunlight surrounding the sun at 8:43 a.m. on the 24th, near Takado, Yamagata City.
Higasa, a ring of light that surrounds the sun, and a phenomenon that seems to be a ring horizontal arc of a rainbow-coloured band of light appeared at the same time in Yamagata City just before 9am on the 24th.
According to the Yamagata Regional Meteorological Observatory, it is a phenomenon that occurs when the sun's light hits the fine ice crystals in the clouds, both in the sun and the horizontal arc.
An ordinary rainbow appears in the opposite direction of the sun, while a circular horizontal ark appears in the same direction as the sun.
It is a relatively common phenomenon, but the circular horizontal ark does not appear as often as the sun.
On that day, they were seen in Takahata-cho.
Chieko Takeda, a 75-year-old housewife in Fukuzawa, was told by her daughter that there was a strange rainbow coming out at about 11 a.m.
“It’s the first time I’ve seen it, and I’m worried that it’s a sign of something bad, but it’s good that I’ve seen something unusual,” he said with a smile.
