Forty-five percent of the households where my wife holds my wallet!
Is my husband happy or unhappy?
"This month's pocket money is not enough . . .", my husband told me, or there is an angry wife, isn't it?
The family where this conversation takes place is the family where the wife holds the wallet.
How many homes do you have in your wallet?
Let’s take a look at the ratio of “couple separate wallets” and “jointly managed”.
Who owns your wallet?
Matsui Securities Co., Ltd. surveyed four hundred men and women in their twenty-thirties (young couples) within three years of marriage nationwide, four hundred men and women in their 50s and 60s who have been married for more than thirty years (mature couples), and a total of eight hundred people.
Do you hold your family’s wallet?
Wife: 45.0% Husband: 24.8% The result was that the family where the wife manages the household is the largest.
No matter who manages it, it seems that there are various episodes, although it is household management that has many twists and turns.
My wife manages the household: Ako-san A-san is a warma of Arafif who has a daughter in the third grade of high school and a daughter in the first year of high school.
Mr. A is in full control of the household budget.
In preparation for the university entrance exam, there were many months when the cram school fee was in deficit, so I negotiated with my husband to lower my pocket money, but of course, I was resisted.
At that time, I was told to "show me what kind of payment is", so I showed my household book.
I should have listed all my expenses, but when I looked at the household accounts, it wasn't enough to make a deficit.
My husband almost leaned on me saying, "It's not enough," but Ako-san said, "I understand, household management is insufficient, so please manage all of them."
Later, when Ms. Ako interviewed her husband, she said, "Even though he is dissatisfied with the management such as pocket money, he does not have the time and energy to manage various households (e.g. school teaching materials, PTA expenses, etc.).
My husband manages the household budget: In the case of Ms. Mr. B, a full-time housewife, is handing out the cost of living by her husband and manages it every day.
In the spring of last year, the freezer part of the refrigerator was broken, so Mr. B asked her husband to buy a refrigerator.
However, my husband said, "I can't use the freezer, but it's okay because I can still use the refrigerated part."
However, in the summer, it seems that I wanted to create an environment where my husband himself can eat ice cream at any time, and his hands turned over, "Let's buy a refrigerator after all".
Therefore, it seems that Mr. B complained to his friend, "My husband is stingy enough".
