On the 25th, the prefecture also revealed the discovery of the bodies of one person, whose gender and age are unknown, were found in a bamboo yabu in Shonaihara, Shonai-cho, the same city.
The body is believed to be one of Watanabe's parents who do not know where to go, and is working to confirm his identity and determine the cause of death.
From midnight on the 7th to the 8th, Mr. Watanabe and others were swept away by the river where the car increased.
Watanabe's body was found near the opposite bank where his grandmother Toshimi, 81, was found.
Disney Announces Postponement of “Moulin” “Avatar” and “Star Wars” (cinemacafe.net) - Yahoo! News
A few days ago in the U.S., where there is no sign of the end of the new coronavirus infection, Warner Bros. has decided to postpone the release of “TENET Tenette” for the third time (indefinite postponement).
[Photo] "Avatar" and "Star Wars" have also been postponed ...
On the 23rd (local time), Disney also announced the postponement of "Mulan" in the form following Warner.
The film was originally scheduled to open nationwide on March 27th, after which the release date was changed to July 24th and August 21st.
“It’s hard to finalize how the film will be released in the last few months in such a global health crisis, so I’d like to pause the release of ‘Moulin’ and think about how we’re going to see it effectively for audiences around the world.”
In addition to "Moulin", there are films that have been postponed at Disney.
"Avatar" is also one of them, which has already passed more than ten months since the previous work.
Director James Cameron posted a letter on Twitter.
“Everything was going well until the outbreak of the new coronavirus, and it was planned to be released in December,” he said, noting that there was a significant delay in the production of the film.
The release of the second "Avatar" will be released in December 2022, one year ahead, the third work is expected to be in 2024, the fourth in 2026, and the fifth is expected to be in 2028.
In addition, the new trilogy of "Star Wars" will be postponed for a year, and the first work will be released in December 2023, the second will be in 2025, and the third will be in 2027.
Kara-mon Gate illuminated by colorful fireworks and light at a nationwide event = Ichijodani Asakura clan ruins in Fukui City, Fukui Prefecture on the night of July 24th
On the evening of July 24th, one year until the opening of the Tokyo Olympics postponed due to the spread of the new coronavirus infection, a nationwide fireworks display event was held by the Japan Youth Chamber (JC) in order to brighten up society as much as possible.
The weather in Fukui Prefecture was unfortunately rainy, but it was launched as scheduled at nine places, coloring the summer night sky.
Overcoming the sense of blockage caused by the spread of infection, JC appealed to each block council across the country and realized it, hoping that it would be a signal that Japan would be reborn.
It starts at 8pm at 117 locations in 46 prefectures at the same time.
At the Ichijodani Asakura clan ruins in Fukui City, a total of 53 2 to 4 balls were launched for about 2 minutes while the surrounding mountains were covered.
With the light of the fireworks, the Karamon Gate and others appeared in the dark night, and it became a fantastic atmosphere.
It was also held on the Matsubara Coast in Tsuruga City and along the Mana River in Ono City.
In order to prevent infection, we did not announce the launch site in advance, hoping to avoid attracting a large number of spectators.
